agentic-code-reviewers v0.4.0 (cursor-sdk)

⚠️ **WARNING:** Authoring-mode validation treats any non-placeholder content under `## Validation & Observation Notes` as sufficient, so a spec with only `### Telemetry & Observable Signals` bullets passes `--mode=authoring` even when `### Negative & Failing Test Scenarios` is absent. That contradicts FORMAT.md, the hardening spec, and the new ac-ledger contract: `negativeScenariosFromSpec()` only ingests the Negative subsection, so init produces an empty `negativeScenarios` array and Step 5 scoring never fail-closes on missing negative coverage. The 0.3.46 TDD gate is therefore bypassable at the front door.

**Correção sugerida:**

```javascript
function negativeScenarioFindings(text) {
  const errors = [];
  const notesHeading = '## Validation & Observation Notes';
  if (!headingPresent(text, notesHeading)) return errors;
  const notesBody = sectionBody(text, notesHeading);
  const subsection = '### Negative & Failing Test Scenarios';
  if (!headingPresent(notesBody, subsection)) {
    errors.push({
      code: 'negative-subsection',
      message: 'Validation & Observation Notes must include ### Negative & Failing Test Scenarios with at least one non-placeholder bullet.',
    });
    return errors;
  }
  const bullets = sectionBody(notesBody, subsection)
    .split('\n')
    .map((line) => line.trim())
    .filter((line) => /^[-*]\s+/.test(line))
    .map((line) => line.replace(/^[-*]\s+/, ''));
  if (!bullets.length || bullets.every((item) => isPlaceholder(item))) {
    errors.push({
      code: 'negative-empty',
      message: '### Negative & Failing Test Scenarios must list at least one expected red test or error state.',
    });
  }
  return errors;
}

// Inside readinessFindings(), after the notes-empty branch:
if (options.mode === 'authoring') errors.push(...negativeScenarioFindings(text));
```

<details>
<summary>🔍 Detalhes da Análise IA</summary>

**Score:** 7/10 | **Ação dev:** fix-code

**Análise:**
1. Evidence: `readinessFindings()` (lines 145–154) only checks heading presence and `sectionIsPlaceholder(sectionBody(...))` for the whole Validation Notes section; it never requires `### Negative & Failing Test Scenarios` or a non-placeholder bullet there. Runtime proof: a telemetry-only fixture passed `validate_spec.cjs --mode=authoring` with exit 0, and `negativeScenariosFromSpec()` returned length 0 when that subsection was omitted while returning length 1 when present. 2. Scenario: An agent writes a new spec with DoR + Telemetry bullets only; Step 0 authoring PASS → `ac_ledger.cjs init` → empty `negativeScenarios` → implement/verify proceed with happy-path ACs only; score can reach ≥ minVerifyScore despite zero red-test contract. 3. Protection: `test/test-validate-spec.js` covers missing DoR, missing Notes, and placeholder Notes, but not telemetry-only Notes without a Negative subsection; `test/test-ac-ledger.js` assumes a spec that already lists a negative scenario. 4. Discards: DoR table lacking an explicit “Failure Modes Defined” row is a separate, softer gap—specs with a proper Negative subsection still flow correctly; this finding is about the telemetry-only bypass, not retired-artifact parity or verify-plan prose (already fixed in prior threads).

**Caminhos analisados:** .agents/skills/ws-spec-format/scripts/validate_spec.cjs, .agents/skills/ws-spec-format/FORMAT.md, .agents/skills/ws-spec-to-pr/scripts/ac_ledger.cjs, .agents/skills/ws-verify-plan/SKILL.md, test/test-validate-spec.js
</details>

